IMPLEMENTATION (SwiftUI + @Observable + KMP facade; adaptive macOS + iOS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
New (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/):
  GlanceModels.swift                value types + pure derivations (vehicle/state/location,
                                    battery tone, location label, command/label maps, phase)
  GlanceFormat.swift                number/range(m→unit)/temp(°C→unit) + freshness formatters
  GlancePageModel.swift             @Observable model + GlanceDataSource seam + load/refresh/send
  GlancePageModel.Sample.swift      Sample/Empty/NoVehicle/Failing data-source doubles
  GlancePage.swift                  View: phase switch + no-vehicle empty + glance column
  GlancePage.Sections.swift         battery gauge, metric card, quick action, status badge,
                                    freshness chip, skeleton
  GlanceRouteRegistration.swift     registers .glance (+ onOpenApp shell hook)
New (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Dashboard/):
  GlancePageModelTests.swift        13 XCTest cases (phases/selection/commands/route/registration)
  GlanceDerivationsTests.swift      14 XCTest cases (isOnline/battery/location/security/format)
Edited:
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift        +case glance (segment "glance", group .overview, icon eye.fill)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift        +GlanceRouteRegistration.registry(base:onOpenApp:)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings +21 keys (20 glance.* + route.glance); additions only
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json     +2 rows (apple-macos + apple-ios, covered==required==30)

Data sources (web parity):
  useVehicles            -> GET /vehicles
  useVehicleState        -> GET /vehicles/{id}/state            (battery_level, rated_range,
                                                                 inside_temp, is_locked,
                                                                 is_climate_on, state)
  useLocationSnapshotLatest -> GET /location-snapshots/latest?vehicle_id
  useVehicleCommand      -> POST /vehicles/{id}/command { command }
  The four web hooks are aggregated behind the `GlanceDataSource` seam (loadVehicles /
  loadState / loadLocation / send), bound through GlancePageModel (no networking in the
  view, ADR-004). The `?vehicle_id` deep-link param resolves the selected vehicle, falling
  back to the first (web `searchParams.get` + `vehicles[0]`). vehicle-list failure is the
  only one that surfaces the retryable error region (web `PageContainer error`); the
  state/location reads fail soft to nil so the page still renders (web `?? '—'`).

SI discipline (ADR-005): rated_range arrives in metres and inside_temp in Celsius (SI on the
  wire). They convert to the user's units ONLY at the render boundary via the shared `Units`
  facade in GlanceFormat.range / .temperature (web `convertDistanceFromSI` /
  `convertTempFromSI`). Nothing non-SI is stored or computed. battery_level (%) is
  unit-independent. The RadialGauge is a native SwiftUI ring (the same primitive the P3
  TSRadialGauge / BatteryRadialGauge use) — never a WKWebView.

