--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two PRE-EXISTING, out-of-scope files are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via
`git status --porcelain` — only the Glance/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp/xcstrings/ledger files
appear) and outside this artifact's allowed files. They fail identically on a clean tree
under the available newer Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6.3 front-end (the repo's macOS verification is
documented PENDING in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md):

  1) apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift
     2x "cannot use explicit 'return' statement in the body of result builder 'ViewBuilder'"
     (lines 88, 101) — inside `#Preview` blocks. Confirmed THE ONLY error: file in a clean
     no-exclusion macOS build (above).
  2) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift
     pre-existing main-actor-isolation diagnostic in the test bundle (see Powershare /
     SleepEfficiency P7 logs).

Both were isolated for THIS page via the command-line build setting
EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES (a build override, no source edits). With them isolated the app
targets build clean on macOS + iOS-Simulator and this page's 27 tests (plus the 8 RouteTests
regression) pass. Code signing was disabled (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO) because no development
certificate exists on this runner — an environment constraint, unrelated to the page. Fixing
the two pre-existing files would breach this artifact's allowed-files scope, so they are left
untouched.

